      "I completed the initial sizing with Aero UP and the Fluent correction, and we flew the first foam-board prototype on November 15. It crashed: it was tail-heavy, its ailerons were too large, and the team was not fully prepared. We cut the aileron area in half, created preflight protocols, and built a second version, which flew in January and February. Flight tests showed poor pitch control on takeoff and a Dutch roll on landing, and we improved the trim and tuned the controls.",
      "![The second foam-board prototype on the pavement](assets/library/deck-prototype-v2.jpg \"Prototype V2, the second foam-board aircraft.\")",
