    "slug": "sae-advanced-shock-load-redesign",
    "group": "sae-aero",
    "season": 2026,
    "title": "SAE Aero Advanced: Integrated Landing Testing",
    "summary": "Testing the interaction between the payload and the aircraft during landing exposed weak points and prompted a redesign.",
    "year": "2025–2026",
    "tags": [
      "Failure analysis",
      "Load testing",
      "Design iteration"
    ],
    "image": "assets/library/adv-payload-final-mat.jpg",
    "imageAlt": "The updated payload on the landing mat, with its lift arm raised",
    "featured": false,
    "overview": [
      "I led the testing for the aircraft, similar to the [testing on the Micro Class](project.html?p=sae-micro-airframe-structure). This caught a failure mode unique to this class, between the payload and the aircraft, during landing.",
      "## What the tests showed",
      "Testing in March showed weak points in the landing gear, the catch mechanism, and the payload lift mechanism, and the April redesign addressed them. The team tested the airframe and the payload for the loads they would see in flight and landing, and after the redesign every component met or exceeded its required load in retesting.",
      "## Landing gear",
      "The original landing gear survived two normal landings in test flights, then failed at its single connection to the lower wing surface. The gear could no longer stand upright, so the aircraft sat at a negative angle of attack. I designed the new gear, which has a second wing attachment and held the aircraft's on-ground position through many high-load cycles ({fig:adv-shock-load-redesign-overview}).",
      "## Catch mechanism",
      "In the integrated drop tests that simulate landing, the original catch mechanism released the payload because of slop between its parts. The new one is completely redesigned: a fixed PLA tray and an actuated blocking arm, with fewer part interfaces and stiffer parts. It keeps the same idea as before, where a mechanical limiter takes the force on the blocker instead of the servo ({fig:adv-shock-load-redesign-overview}).",
      "![The old and new landing gear on the aircraft, and the old and new catch mechanism](assets/library/adv-shock-load-redesign-overview.jpg \"The old and new landing gear (top) and catch mechanism (bottom). The new designs are the ones flown at the competition.\")",
      "## Lift mechanism",
      "The lift mechanism ({fig:adv-lift-mechanism}) failed from shock loading during landing. The fix was to make the base plate from aluminum and to print the interface between the lift mechanism and the frame in TPU, with an improved joint between the two. The TPU is ductile and helps dissipate the load of a landing. The new lift mechanism also lifts 0.4 in higher, which gives more room for variation during real operations. We tested the new design again to confirm the strength. The redesign was the payload team's work. I ran the tests that prompted it and the retests, and I printed many of the parts.",
      "![The payload in a lowered position on the ground and a raised position attached to the aircraft](assets/library/adv-lift-mechanism.png \"The payload lift mechanism, lowered (on the ground) and raised (attached to the aircraft).\")"
    ],
